WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.800
The evals-first LLMOps loop.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.639
Software has unit tests.

3
00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:09.000
LLM systems have this loop, and it makes everything else changeable.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.267
The phrase to own: if you can't measure it, you can't ship it.

5
00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:18.600
Every prompt tweak, model upgrade and retrieval change flows through the same circle.

6
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.800
Here is the loop.

7
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.767
It starts with a golden set of trusted questions.

8
00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.667
A CI gate runs it against every change.

9
00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:30.567
Passing changes go to a canary, a small share of traffic.

10
00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:32.667
Traces log every request.

11
00:00:32.967 --> 00:00:36.900
A judge scores a sample of them, and the failures it finds are mined.

12
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.200
Those failures become new golden questions, so the set keeps growing.

13
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.033
Offline and online evals do different jobs.

14
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:48.600
The offline suite catches regressions before deploy.

15
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:55.733
Online judging catches what the golden set does not cover yet, on a sample of one to five percent of traffic.

16
00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:59.700
Together they should cost single-digit percent of your inference spend.

17
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.733
An LLM judge is not automatically right.

18
00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.333
First, collect human labels on a sample.

19
00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.233
Then calibrate the judge against them every quarter.

20
00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:12.167
And watch for position and verbosity bias.

21
00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.833
Here is a change in flight.

22
00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:18.767
A prompt is edited and the golden-set suite runs in CI.

23
00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:22.233
It wins, so a canary sends five percent of traffic to it.

24
00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:26.533
If the online judge sees quality drop, it rolls back automatically.

25
00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:28.359
Let's recap.

26
00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:30.600
If you can't measure it, you can't ship it.

27
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.733
One loop handles every change.

28
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:35.267
Offline and online evals both matter.

29
00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:38.023
And calibrate your judge against humans.

30
00:01:38.023 --> 00:01:40.233
Next up: the streaming chat backend.
